HST Office: ribbon groups of the 1.0.3 (v3) design laid out by the owner-locked mockup's own rules.

- vcl/inc/HstRibbonV3Pack.hxx (new, plain arithmetic, unit tested by tests/unit/test_ribbon_v3_pack.py against the
  mockup's packItems()/packRun()/eff() for all 329 groups of data/ribbon/ribbon-v3.json at every state): the look of
  every command of a group at a state (L large, M small with its label, S icon only; a sparse tab's fill pass makes
  a group large; Paste and a one-command group stay large), its blocks from left to right (large buttons and
  galleries in their order, the small commands as one run where the first stands: balanced columns of at most 3,
  4 = 2 + 2, or 1-3 rows beside a large button so the run reaches the bottom row; a group's fixed 3-row layout) and
  their positions (rows at 0/26/52, 24 high; large buttons and galleries 76 high; 4 px between blocks; one width
  for the labelled buttons and boxes of a group's columns; the tab's one large-button width), scaled to device px.
- vcl/source/control/HstRibbonV3Layout.cxx (new): a GtkGrid with "hst-ribbon-layout" (hst-ribbon-v3-ui.patch) is a
  v3 group; VclGrid's requisition and allocation place its commands by the plan instead of by its cells: 6 px
  padding, content 76 px high 6 px under the top, the caption band 18 px (or the caption's height) 4 px under the
  content, the separator at the right edge. A command's look is applied to its toolbox (button type, size, text
  position; the only button stretched over its cell: ToolBox::HstSetStretch), menu button (large: image above the
  label, ▾ ending its second line; medium: image beside it; small: image only) or gallery (hst-gallery-state).
  Natural widths are measured once per look. HST_RIBBON_DUMP_LAYOUT=<dir> writes the layout of every tab as JSON
  (tests/runtime/check-ribbon-v3-dumps.py).
- PriorityMergedHBox: a box whose groups are all v3 fits them by the mockup's fit(): all large; on a tab more than
  40 % free the groups turn large from the left, then every large button widens to 96; the tab's large buttons
  share the narrowest even width of 52 to 96 that fits their labels; when too wide the galleries go M then S and
  the groups go M, S, then "Caption ▾" from the right; what still does not fit folds into the chevron. The fit
  uses the width beside the smallest banner, so the banner growing into free room changes no group.
- The banner (NotebookbarTabControl): never hidden, 360 to 960 logical px wide, 96 high at the groups' top, 8 px
  after the last group (it takes the room the groups leave); old 360 x 104 artwork takes its height at the left
  and the colour of its right edge fills the rest.
- The ribbon tooltip ends with the owner's single KeyTip hint: "Alt+Q, type the command's name".

